{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "route": {
    "route_id": "syria-trunk",
    "name": "Damascus-Aleppo Railway (Syrian trunk)",
    "name_arabic": "سكة حديد دمشق-حلب",
    "countries": "Syria",
    "gauge_mm": 1435,
    "year_opened": 1983,
    "era": "historic",
    "color": "#b45309",
    "corridor_confidence": "high",
    "description": "Syrian standard-gauge north-south trunk; the connector to Aleppo",
    "notes": "The internal Syrian standard-gauge trunk; the physical link from the Levant routes to the Baghdad Railway.  [established] The Homs-Hama-Aleppo section is the DHP standard-gauge northern line (opened 1902-1906); the DIRECT Damascus-Homs standard-gauge link (194 km) opened only in 1983 (before that Damascus connected north via Rayak / the narrow gauge). So the full through trunk dates variously 1906-1983.  [connections] This is the missing SPINE that ties the network together: it meets the Beirut-Damascus and Hejaz lines at Damascus; the Rayak-Baalbek and Tripoli-Homs lines at Homs; the Syrian coastal and Euphrates lines; and the Baghdad Railway at Aleppo (-> Turkey and Iraq). GSGS 2061/9 (1916): trunk drawn as COMPLETED railway. Note: the 1916 map routes Damascus↔Homs via Rayak/Baalbek (the direct An-Nabk alignment we model postdates 1916) — An-Nabk not shown on the 1916 trunk; Maarat al-Numan drawn as a town, not a station on the line. Era corrected 2026-07-25: the direct Damascus–An-Nabk(–Dumayr)–Homs line opened 1983 (CFS network map; Syria's 1969–1990 build-out), not 1906. The Homs–Hama–Aleppo section is the older DHP standard gauge (~1906), shared with the pre-1983 Rayak-routed trunk (modeled via beirut-damascus + rayak-baalbek→Homs). Alignment corrected 2026-07-26 (syrische-eisenbahn.de CFS section table + syrianheritage_gdr_railway GDR account + Wikipedia 'Rail transport in Syria'; reconciled via the Levantrain Damascus–Aleppo research pass): the 1983 Damascus–Homs line runs the EASTERN DESERT via Dumayr→Mhin (1980 Homs–Mhin phosphate branch, extended to Damascus 1983), NOT the M5 via An-Nabk/Qara. Terminus = Qadam (SG intercity; the city Hejaz station is closed to traffic). Removed An-Nabk (M5 inference, no rail basis) and Maarat al-Numan (highway town W of the line; Hama–Aleppo runs E of Jabal Zawiya via Abu al-Duhur). Damascus–Homs kept SCHEMATIC (settlement-proxy coords off the rail; passing loops need satellite survey). CFS 2010/2011 timetables list ~zero intermediate stops Damascus–Homs → intermediate points are station_exists, not necessarily station_served.",
    "history": "The standard-gauge (1,435 mm) spine of the Syrian network. Its northern half (Homs-Hama-Aleppo) is the French DHP 'prolongements' opened 1902-1906; the Damascus-Homs section was completed as standard gauge in 1983, giving a continuous Damascus-Aleppo trunk.",
    "verification_status": "unverified",
